# Read under Linux, where a carriage return ends up inside a command or a hash: the measurement's
# copy of the pins, which `env.sh` reads, and the batch files, whose last word on a line would
# otherwise carry one into `run-op.sh`. The root rules cover `*.sh`, `*.flow`, `*.py` and the root
# `android.sha256` only.
scripts/android.sha256 text eol=lf
scripts/batches/*.txt text eol=lf
# The later measurements' batch files, which `batch-ow.sh` and `batch-sy.sh` read the same way.
scripts/batches-ow/*.txt text eol=lf
# The same for the two measurements of 2026-11-16, each in a directory of its own.
scripts/keepassdx/android.sha256 text eol=lf
scripts/keepassdx/batches/*.txt text eol=lf
scripts/k2a-background/batches-ow/*.txt text eol=lf

# The checksums rclone publishes, kept as they arrived: a signed text, whose bytes stay as signed.
recorded/k2a-synchronize/server/SHA256SUMS -text

# The MD5 pair is two bodies whose digests are quoted, so they are bytes, not text.
*.bin binary
